       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for ibuprofen, which is 3,200 mg/day in a monitored setting.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg per administration is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up substantially. Kidney and liver function are normal, but that doesn't make this dose safe.\n\nTypical regimens are:\n- **Anti-inflammatory or analgesic:** 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours, with a maximum of 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed, usually capped at 1,200 mg/day for OTC-style use.\n\nDid you mean 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or 1600 mg per day in divided doses? Tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale. I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
